Third-party code vendored in the component repositories
-------------------------------------------------------

sdkjs, common/clientpdf/vendor/fontkit: @pdf-lib/fontkit 1.1.1 (fork of
fontkit by Devon Govett and Andrew Dillon), MIT, unmodified; the bundle also
contains restructure, unicode-properties, unicode-trie, brotli (decoder),
tiny-inflate, pako, dfa, clone, base64-js, buffer (MIT or zlib) and ieee754
(BSD-3-Clause). The LICENSE and README sit next to the file.

document-server-integration, web-apps/documentserver-example/.../elixir/fluent:
Microsoft Fluent UI System Icons subset (MIT), with its LICENSE.

server, AdminPanel/.../ai/vendor: GPT-3-Encoder, markdown-it and select2
(MIT), with their licence files.

The WebAssembly converter is built from the "core" component with the
Emscripten toolchain and small patches kept in tools/wasm/patches/; its
upstream licences (AGPL-3.0 for core, and those of the libraries it embeds)
are unchanged.

Node.js and Python packages used by the build and the tests (Electron,
electron-builder, Playwright, Pillow, NumPy, SciPy, scikit-image, OpenCV,
python-docx, lxml, openpyxl, python-pptx, ...) are installed from their
registries and are not redistributed in this repository; each keeps its own
licence.
